WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:02.537
This code demonstrates the idea of creating

00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:04.866
and importing your own module directly inside

00:00:04.879 --> 00:00:08.342
the browser Because this interactive lesson runs

00:00:08.355 --> 00:00:11.145
in a browser-based Python environment the example

00:00:11.171 --> 00:00:13.263
first creates the contents of a module

00:00:13.289 --> 00:00:16.882
as text That text contains two functions

00:00:17.803 --> 00:00:21.197
The first function is calculate profit It

00:00:21.224 --> 00:00:23.842
receives sales and costs then returns sales

00:00:23.868 --> 00:00:27.303
minus costs The second function is profit

00:00:27.329 --> 00:00:31.039
margin It first calls calculate profit then

00:00:31.066 --> 00:00:34.092
divides the profit by sales This is

00:00:34.118 --> 00:00:36.395
a good example of one function reusing

00:00:36.421 --> 00:00:39.618
another function Next the code opens a

00:00:39.645 --> 00:00:41.921
file named calculations dot P Y in

00:00:41.947 --> 00:00:43.724
write mode and writes the module text

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:46.500
into that file At this point a

00:00:46.526 --> 00:00:48.724
real Python module file exists in the

00:00:48.737 --> 00:00:52.632
browser's temporary Python environment The code then

00:00:52.645 --> 00:00:55.895
imports importlib and imports the calculations
module

00:00:56.829 --> 00:00:58.895
Importlib dot reload is used so that

00:00:58.921 --> 00:01:00.487
if you edit the module text and

00:01:00.513 --> 00:01:02.737
run the cell again Python reloads the

00:01:02.763 --> 00:01:06.132
updated version After that sales is set

00:01:06.158 --> 00:01:08.079
to fifteen hundred and costs is set

00:01:08.105 --> 00:01:11.250
to eleven hundred The first print statement

00:01:11.276 --> 00:01:15.447
calls calculations dot calculate profit The expected

00:01:15.474 --> 00:01:18.579
profit is four hundred The second print

00:01:18.605 --> 00:01:22.645
statement calls calculations dot profit margin Four

00:01:22.658 --> 00:01:25.276
hundred divided by fifteen hundred is approximately

00:01:25.303 --> 00:01:27.342
zero point two six seven when rounded

00:01:27.368 --> 00:01:30.526
to three decimal places Click Run now

00:01:30.539 --> 00:01:33.342
and check the terminal output You should

00:01:33.368 --> 00:01:35.513
see Profit followed by four hundred and

00:01:35.539 --> 00:01:38.289
Profit margin followed by approximately zero point

00:01:38.303 --> 00:01:41.197
two six seven Now change sales to

00:01:41.211 --> 00:01:43.566
two thousand and costs to sixteen hundred

00:01:44.487 --> 00:01:47.342
Run the code again The profit is

00:01:47.368 --> 00:01:49.618
still four hundred but the profit margin

00:01:49.632 --> 00:01:51.434
changes because four hundred is now a

00:01:51.447 --> 00:01:54.750
smaller percentage of total sales This is

00:01:54.776 --> 00:01:58.053
an important idea A module lets us

00:01:58.079 --> 00:02:01.118
separate reusable formulas from the main analysis

00:02:02.039 --> 00:02:04.500
In a real project calculations dot P

00:02:04.526 --> 00:02:06.013
Y and main dot P Y would

00:02:06.039 --> 00:02:08.224
usually be separate files in the project

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:08.697
folder
